<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary operations.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary operations.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico completed all three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements it had offered in order to drain 1.999 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    349 days   20.86 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   20.89 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   19.91 pct</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     46 days   19.41 pct</p>
<p>    700 million     38 days   19.42 pct</p>
<p>    300 million	6 days   18.53 pct</p>
<p>    149 million	3 days   18.15 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City Newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
